config BR2_PACKAGE_ASCENT_VENDOR_FIRMWARE
	bool "ascent-vendor-firmware"
	help
	  Fetches and extracts CADDX's "Ascent H Sky" vendor OTA image
	  exactly once, straight into BINARIES_DIR (output/images/
	  ar8030.img, output/images/sensors/*.bin), for hi3516cv6xx_fpv_
	  caddx-ascent-lite's ar8030 (baseband demo firmware) and waybeam
	  (os02k10 sensor tuning) packages to each copy what they need out
	  of and install themselves -- see extract.py's docstring for the
	  full story, including why only the raw vendor zip/img itself
	  (cache/vendor-images/, shared and surviving builder.sh's
	  `rm -rf openipc`) needs persistent caching, not these extracted
	  artifacts.

	  Not meant to be enabled by hand: hi3516cv6xx_fpv_caddx-ascent-
	  lite's defconfig turns this on directly, and ar8030's/waybeam's
	  own FETCH_DEPENDENCY string options (see those packages'
	  Config.in) name it so Buildroot's scheduler builds it first.
	  Single-device-specific by design, same as this repo's
	  kc110-board-support -- not something another AR8030/waybeam
	  board would select unless it also happens to use this exact
	  vendor image.
